{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1378841-prometheus-chamber-replication","id":1378841,"title":"Prometheus Chamber Replication","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: \u00c6on"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-04-05T14:10:18-07:00","id":1378841,"title":"Prometheus Chamber Replication","content":"Sooo I was wondering if there was a way for Psions to replicate the Promtheus Chambers so that there can be more than one of each type of them. That and can they make a sort of Super-Prometheus Chamber that basically can create a psion of any type rather than being specific to a particular Aptitude. (I do know that chambers can be fixed, healed really, as proven by the destroyed QK chamber coming back after years of work).<br /> <br /> The reason I ask this is because I had the idea of a campaign where a bunch of psions (and secretly not so secretly psiads) decide that they don't want to stay on Earth and so 'steal' a Leviathan and leave. If they are able to have chambers with them then they can be self-sustaining but if they don't then they need to still keep a connection with Earth and the psi orders. (Though as I think on things in greater detail writing this post that might not be the worst thing, having to keep an eye and ear and some hands on Earth could be interesting plot points.)<br /> <br /> As an aside an alternate way to go about doing this is to create an alternate Aeon Setting where the Psions are servants (really slaves) of the governmental system that dominates Earth and her immediate colonies. In order to escape the hold the Terran Peoples Republic have over them a number of psions and psiads (and talents as well) work together to sabotage the government, steal the Prometheus Chambers, and seize the new prototype mega-Leviathan (which is capable of traveling to stars farther out then the current ones due to some mcguffin) in order for them, their families, and their friends to escape the totalitarian grip of Earth government.<br /> <br /> I could see Aeon Society being at the center of the operations designed to gather the rebel psions together in order to make the whole escape possible. These rebel leaders would be the ones that would lay at the heart of the new psi orders that would be formed during the rebellion and made more firm during the travel to a new home. (While most orders could stay the same some changes to the Ministry would have to occur as a government body wouldn't really work in this version of Aeon.) <br /> <br /> Anyway, let me stop here before I go on and make an essay that goes far beyond my basic question - which is can additional Prometheus Chambers be created.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-05T14:20:50-07:00","id":1378843,"title":"","content":"Officially, the Orders have monopolies on the various kinds of Psions, and they have their monopolies because of the uniqueness of the Prometheus Chambers. So no, they can't be replicated or modified. <br /> <br /> Of course, a good chunk of that is a holdover where it was assumed that Order and Aptitude were joined at the hip. In 2e, I would have no problem house ruling it to say that Prometheus Chambers are difficult to copy, and the copies are inferior to the original (largely in being slower and thus not able to activate as many Scions, and not being copyable themselves). And alterations would still be impossible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-05T15:18:17-07:00","id":1378854,"title":"","content":"Presumably when humanity takes control of their own evolution, that tech is in their future. In the early 22nd century, no one has any idea how to make new Prometheus Chambers yet. Even SK\u2019s reconstruction of her chamber required use of the Doyen provided core that survived the assault. So the answer to \u201cis it possible?\u201d - yes, the Chambers are tech and humans given full understanding and tools will be able to engineer them just as the Doyen do. But no one has achieved that knowledge yet and it will be a major plot point when they do.<br /> <br /> Hey... you know who would be helpful toward this end? Mega-Intellect Novas. Almost like overcoming the Doyen\u2019s leash requires humanity (and other sapients) overcoming their animosities and uniting and that\u2019s a central theme of the game...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 04-06-2020, 06:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-05T15:30:26-07:00","id":1378857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1378841-prometheus-chamber-replication?p=1378843#post1378843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Officially, the Orders have monopolies on the various kinds of Psions, and they have their monopolies because of the uniqueness of the Prometheus Chambers. So no, they can't be replicated or modified.<br /> <br /> Of course, a good chunk of that is a holdover where it was assumed that Order and Aptitude were joined at the hip. In 2e, I would have no problem house ruling it to say that Prometheus Chambers are difficult to copy, and the copies are inferior to the original (largely in being slower and thus not able to activate as many Scions, and not being copyable themselves). And alterations would still be impossible.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right now Prometheus Chambers - the core process of them - are Black Box technology. Yeah, they activate Psion, but we have no idea how. Figure is a few decade - perhaps with the aid of friendly Mega-Int Novas humans will crack the process, but that's probably something that's going to wait for Trinity Continuum: Away the hell in the future.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-05T15:48:31-07:00","id":1378865,"title":"","content":"For what it's worth, my point had less to do with that and more to do with \u201call Telepaths come from the Ministry's Prometheus Chamber; all Clairsentients came from ISRA's Prometheus Chamber; all Electrokinetics come from Orgotek's Prometheus Chamber; etc.\u201d Given that every Order has Psions with every Aptitude, they either have an exchange program going on or each Order has a way to activate any Aptitude.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 04-05-2020, 06:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-05T23:03:41-07:00","id":1378928,"title":"","content":"The Doyen would oppose any attempt, and I do honestly believe that officially sanctioned attempts would be requested, if not enforced.<br /> Heck, I can see the Psi Orders wanting to have a spare/secondary chamber.<br /> <br /> The problem is, no one has a solid lead on duplicating/replicating key components of Doyen design.<br /> That said, I do think it is the kind of thing Palket would love to study and be involved with. Would probably result in a meteor to the face though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-05T23:19:09-07:00","id":1378930,"title":"","content":"Trinity 1e has a passage where the Qin give humans a piece of biotech as a gift. The humans grab it, run off, study it for weeks. Can't make heads or tails of it. It's too complex. They come back, hat in hand, and say &quot;we can't figure this out. Can you tell us what it is?&quot; The Qin look confused, and say &quot;it's a vase.&quot;<br /> <br /> Now imagine a level of biotech that makes the Qin scratch their heads.<br /> <br /> That's basically what we're dealing with in the Prometheus Chambers.<br /> <br /> Is it <i>possible</i> for humans to figure them out? Absolutely. Have they yet? No.<br /> <br /> The Psi Orders guard them jealously: if you do accidentally something to break one, you've essentially killed off that order's future prospects for recruitment. When even their location is a closely-guarded secret, they're definitely not going to let just <i>anyone</i> examine them. You have to be <i>extremely</i> well-trusted by the proxies to even get a chance, and even then, dunking a new psion takes priority, so your time is going to be limited. And any research is probably going to be slapped under an NDA, exclusive to that Order.<br /> <br /> The number of people who have had a chance to examine any single tank is few. The number who have had a chance to examine more than one tank can probably be counted on one hand.<br /> <br /> It's probably going to take some time for researchers examining and comparing at least three different tanks before they can learn enough to start growing a brand new tank of their own. It's a challenging task, but not impossible, and perhaps even doable by an enterprising group of PCs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-06T03:18:23-07:00","id":1378964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1378841-prometheus-chamber-replication?p=1378865#post1378865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For what it's worth, my point had less to do with that and more to do with \u201call Telepaths come from the Ministry's Prometheus Chamber; all Clairsentients came from ISRA's Prometheus Chamber; all Electrokinetics come from Orgotek's Prometheus Chamber; etc.\u201d Given that every Order has Psions with every Aptitude, they either have an exchange program going on or each Order has a way to activate any Aptitude.</div> </div> </div> </div>They have an exchange program. AEon facilitates most of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-06T12:57:30-07:00","id":1379039,"title":"","content":"While this does make me want to a) destroy the Doyen and b) find a way to increase psiad numbers and strength it also makes me quite intrigued at the future of the setting. <br /> <br /> Soooo in some ways a better campaign potential is for the group to, on their external adventurers in outer space, find ancient ruins or something that could aid them in either increasing the rate of psiad manifestation or lets them develop alternatives to the Prometheus chamber. <br /> <br /> As a random question I wonder which Proxies would best agree to actions that work to against the mysterious plans of beings outside of humanity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-07T03:38:53-07:00","id":1379207,"title":"","content":"So I figure the Prometheus Chambers are just hard to replicate but nothing is impossible. The thing is it represents higher levels of tech secretly given to a lower tech level civ. So if people weren't Busy with several Armageddon's they could attempt to replicate facets of the Prometheus Chamber idea. Like I wager they will first maybe try to crack the tech and make a chamber but the prototypes would be weaker, but perhaps without the secret genlocks and traps the Doyen built in, this is a situation where somebody tries to replicate the chamber with only some data on them rather then having access to them fully. I'm thinking a situation like a splinter group of Psions, Scientists, and Talents like stealing the known data on the Chambers and trying to replicate it after they Wormhole jump away from earth. The Downside is it probably won't be as powerful and reliable (remember the Doyen can do even more since when given the prep they custom gene surgeried the first Batch of Psions into Proxies) but since they would be missing a lot of crucial data and are essentially reinventing them they wouldn't be including the Doyen failsafes and species control methods. They may make machines that actually make Psiads rather then Psions because of this. It probably also would be something that takes a bit more resources and prep per individual.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-07T07:01:37-07:00","id":1379248,"title":"","content":"To be fair, a machine that makes psiads would be quite an achievement. As this stand, the public consists of three kinds of people where psionics are concerned: baselines, latents, and psiads. A baseline will only ever be a baseline; sticking one in a Prometheus Chamber will do nothing <i>at best</i>, same with a psiad. Putting a latent in a Prometheus Chamber gives you a psion. <br /> <br /> Because of their comparative versatility, psiads are not \u201clesser psions\u201d; and given sufficient evolution of the psiads as a whole, you might eventually (in a hundred years or so?) see psiads who can attain the power that psions currently have \u2014 at which point the <i>psions</i> will have to have developed some new edge or else be considered the \u201csecond class psionics\u201d. <br /> <br /> Now, you're of course free to do whatever you want in your own games; the point here isn't to say \u201cdon't do it\u201d in terms of putting a ninth Prometheus Chamber on a starship. Rather, it's to point out what is the impact on the setting of doing so, and why it hasn't happened before. If you do it, it's because there's something very unusual going on with your ship \u2014 something that's unlikely to be replicable. Your ship might have a Tony Stark style Nova on board who built and continues to maintain and operate this \u201cninth Chamber\u201d as a bit of Nova-Tech that can <i>only</i> be operated by him; or the ship may have uncovered a ninth Prometheus Chamber core on one of the first worlds they visited, with no idea where it came from out how it got there. Either way, if word of what they have gets out, they're going to be in the spotlight of international attention like you've never seen before. It's \u201cwell, we want to cut ties with Earth; so let's build a Promethean Chamber\u201d. <br /> <br /> To draw an analogy, it would be kind of like a 19th-century warship's crew deciding that they want to arm themselves with a Nuke.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 04-07-2020, 10:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-07T08:24:20-07:00","id":1379257,"title":"","content":"While I agree a Mega Intelligent Nova would help, the nature of Psi and Quantum make impossible for a Nova to develop a chamber because it\u2019s one of the few things that is out of their reach (and probably time and dimension travel), they just can\u2019t handle the noetic template handling needed. A Mega Intelligent Nova would be really helpful on helping Psions/Psiads on the job, creating the genetic manipulation part, and maybe help identifying and duplicating the physical part of the process, while the others focus on the gnostic template part.<br /> <br /> I know a Superior can create Inspired Psionic Items, and I would say a Nova can do that too, But I don\u2019t know if a Nova can do a Powered Psionic tech, even worse, a rank 7 (or 8) item like a Prometheus chamber.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-07T08:38:02-07:00","id":1379258,"title":"","content":"We know gravity exists. We can see the effects of gravity. We can measure the effects of gravity. But we can't SEE gravity. We can't sense it directly. I would expect a nova to be able to do something similar with noetics. If they know it exists, they can probably figure out a way to work with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-07T09:18:52-07:00","id":1379260,"title":"","content":"Probably not on their own, though. Figure that our genius Nova would need to team up with a proxy-level psion to do this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-07T09:23:24-07:00","id":1379261,"title":"","content":"We could always have had pre-Aeon SK work with a nova on the development of something that while not a Prometheus Chamber could work in a similar way. Maybe, right before the whole situation with the Doyen appeared her memories of that deal were erased - maybe at her choosing. Our band of player heroes could be sent to chase certain clues that would lead to the treasure trove of her ancient work.<br /> <br /> By the way I am all for the idea that a Mega-Int Nova could create something that works to manipulate psi forces even though he himself can't directly touch it. <br /> <br /> I am also open to the potential of there being the potential for something in certain psiads that when they get dunked into a prometheus chamber they don't come out psion or unchanged they instead come out super-psiad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":661,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","user":"LordHeru","date":". 04-07-2020, 12:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-07T19:51:55-07:00","id":1379381,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1378841-prometheus-chamber-replication?p=1379248#post1379248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be fair, a machine that makes psiads would be quite an achievement. As this stand, the public consists of three kinds of people where psionics are concerned: baselines, latents, and psiads. A baseline will only ever be a baseline; sticking one in a Prometheus Chamber will do nothing <i>at best</i>, same with a psiad. Putting a latent in a Prometheus Chamber gives you a psion.<br /> <br /> Because of their comparative versatility, psiads are not \u201clesser psions\u201d; and given sufficient evolution of the psiads as a whole, you might eventually (in a hundred years or so?) see psiads who can attain the power that psions currently have \u2014 at which point the <i>psions</i> will have to have developed some new edge or else be considered the \u201csecond class psionics\u201d.<br /> <br /> Now, you're of course free to do whatever you want in your own games; the point here isn't to say \u201cdon't do it\u201d in terms of putting a ninth Prometheus Chamber on a starship. Rather, it's to point out what is the impact on the setting of doing so, and why it hasn't happened before. If you do it, it's because there's something very unusual going on with your ship \u2014 something that's unlikely to be replicable. Your ship might have a Tony Stark style Nova on board who built and continues to maintain and operate this \u201cninth Chamber\u201d as a bit of Nova-Tech that can <i>only</i> be operated by him; or the ship may have uncovered a ninth Prometheus Chamber core on one of the first worlds they visited, with no idea where it came from out how it got there. Either way, if word of what they have gets out, they're going to be in the spotlight of international attention like you've never seen before. It's \u201cwell, we want to cut ties with Earth; so let's build a Promethean Chamber\u201d.<br /> <br /> To draw an analogy, it would be kind of like a 19th-century warship's crew deciding that they want to arm themselves with a Nuke.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wasn't implying they were lesser Psions, they wouldn't have all the backdoors built into them by the Doyen and they would be of a free destiny. I was just saying they would get a product, and remember I would wager they didn't even know Psiads existed since they only probably know of Psions being the first psychics. They would think Psiads were new beings that operated on similar principles, sacrifice narrow mastery for broader versatility and competence. Their was talk that in the future after the Aeon Era when Doyen are beaten and humanity is free to make their own Destiny we wouldn't have Psions, at least not as they are so we probably would have Psiads and maybe Psions minus secret backdoor noetic boobytraps.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-07T20:26:31-07:00","id":1379389,"title":"","content":"Hey all thanks for the all ideas! <br /> <br /> Honestly, thinking about it, minus a whole setting change the 'better' (in the sense of more fun) idea is totally NOT giving the group in the intro post access to their own chamber but making them a mix of Psiads and Psions who joined up with them. The fact that they still need Earth - and the Orders - in order to increase their numbers beyond the slow growth of psiads means that Earth is still important, giving them a reason to keep in contact with said world and the problems going on. <br /> <br /> I also like the ideas of a Nova helping them create alternate Prometheus Chambers and the potential of some alien ruin having something that could serve as either a similar function or the kernel of a new version. <br /> <br /> The fact that Prometheus Chambers are highly complex, multifaceted pieces of psionic bioware is also something that I need to not just ignore and stuff, hehe. <br /> <br /> I do have to say in an aside that the many comments here do very much make me interesting in the potential saga where the PCs are the ones to go through a series of adventurers to where they uncover certain secrets that work to free the Orders from certain limitations of their formation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-07T20:33:33-07:00","id":1379391,"title":"","content":"By the way, superiors wouldn't be any help in creating a Prometheus chamber. They can't do the equivalent of Nova-Tech where are biotech is concerned, only the lesser two stages.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-07T20:47:32-07:00","id":1379395,"title":"","content":"It is kind of weird that Quantum beings can't even work on Noetic Concepts and Noetic Beings can't even really grock Quantum. I understand why they did it but sometimes its comes off weird where you have just a super intelligent bloke and its not just he can't build a replicated tech he can't even understand the designs.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1378841-prometheus-chamber-replication?p=1379391#post1379391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By the way, superiors wouldn't be any help in creating a Prometheus chamber. They can't do the equivalent of Nova-Tech where are biotech is concerned, only the lesser two stages.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean Super intelligent people would always be useful, even if they themselves can't lead the research.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-07T20:53:21-07:00","id":1379396,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1378841-prometheus-chamber-replication?p=1379395#post1379395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is kind of weird that Quantum beings can't even work on Noetic Concepts and Noetic Beings can't even really grock Quantum. I understand why they did it but sometimes its comes off weird where you have just a super intelligent bloke and its not just he can't build a replicated tech he can't even understand the designs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well this isn't entirely true as it seems its permissible for Psions to touch Nova stuff but not for Novas to touch Psion stuff, as shown by QK in Aeon and the sidebars about mental powers in the Aberrant kickstarter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-07T21:16:57-07:00","id":1379401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1378841-prometheus-chamber-replication?p=1379396#post1379396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well this isn't entirely true as it seems its permissible for Psions to touch Nova stuff but not for Novas to touch Psion stuff, as shown by QK in Aeon and the sidebars about mental powers in the Aberrant kickstarter.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a step in the right direction! Yeah mundane slowly work their way into making Supertechnology real.<br /> <br /> Hey then it seems at some point though Psi tech becomes mundane, and then at that point Novas can probably create it and understand those examples. Like when the tech hits mainstream and is easily mass produced rather then in a situation where an advanced megacorp or a government are the only ones able to make it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-07T21:37:05-07:00","id":1379404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1378841-prometheus-chamber-replication?p=1379396#post1379396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well this isn't entirely true as it seems its permissible for Psions to touch Nova stuff but not for Novas to touch Psion stuff, as shown by QK in Aeon and the sidebars about mental powers in the Aberrant kickstarter.</div> </div> </div> </div>The fact that a Superior Inventor can mess with noetic inventions suggests that the ability to manipulate the other does go both ways.<br /> <br /> That said, the level of noetic super science that Superiors are unable to mess with is the powered tech. It has long been established that even with Nova-Tech, even other Novas have trouble making heads or tails of it until the inventor puts in some effort to make it \u201ceasier to understand\u201d. There is an implication at the very least that with powered tech there is more going on than just \u201cam I smart enough to understand the blueprints?\u201d <br /> <br /> At least in the first stages of its development, a powered invention isn't doing what it does all by itself; it works more as a channel for the inventor's power. Subsequent development makes the powered item more independent from the inventor, at first making it easier for other Novas to use it, then making it possible for other Novas to duplicate it. At <i>that</i> point, it's arguably in the realm of \u201cam I smart enough to understand this?\u201d and everything after that is just a matter of turning it into Inspired Science and then Advanced Science.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 04-08-2020, 12:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-08T04:30:31-07:00","id":1379445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1378841-prometheus-chamber-replication?p=1379404#post1379404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The fact that a Superior Inventor can mess with noetic inventions suggests that the ability to manipulate the other does go both ways.</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn\u2019t. Superiors aren\u2019t Quantum. They\u2019re essentially triggered sub-Quantum potential that\u2019s locked off while it\u2019s still inspiration powered and doesn\u2019t approach anything near actual Quantum power.<br /> <br /> As soon as actual Quantum enters the mix, you lose the ability to work with all aspects of noetic tech. A mega-intelligence nova might be able to understand some genetic recombination effects that Prometheus Chambers perform - if someone gives the nova schematics or blueprints, because if he actually interacts with it the chamber\u2019s going to get sick and possibly die - but the nova will have no awareness of the noetic reshaping that it does in parallel. Even if someone explains the effect and outcome he can\u2019t make the connections because it\u2019s an absolute blind spot to him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-08T04:46:31-07:00","id":1379450,"title":"","content":"Just to complete Dataweaver post about Superiors.<br /> <br /> Superiors still have a Psi value of 1, it means they are still capable of interacting with psi as humans can. A Nova does not have Psi at all, their quantum is so strong it disrupt completely the psi trait.<br /> <br /> Also, Inspired tech is usable by anyone, and probably easier to invent as cross-source, as it uses an external source and so become more physical.<br /> <br /> Q-Tech and Noetic powered items are a different thing, it requires more than understanding. A nova can build q-tech out of sticks and brute quantum, as it don\u2019t require special materials and things like that, his power shapes the reality of the invention and make it work basically. We probably can say the same about Noetic powered tech, the base for construction is physical, BUT the workings are not, it works on a psi realm, that novas can\u2019t manipulate at all, of course, Psions work in a lower scale, so they require more refined physical structure to handle the noetic part (biotech and crystals).<br /> <br /> As we are talking about Super Tech. The way they used to creating Supertrch in Aexpansion is far superior to the way it works on Aberrant. Easier to pick the effects and flaws. While I like the way flaws are forced in the creation process described in Core, when a player create a new item, giving a flaw to the item is optional and have no advantage at all (not even momentum generation).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-08T05:09:52-07:00","id":1379455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1378841-prometheus-chamber-replication?p=1379450#post1379450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A nova can build q-tech out of sticks and brute quantum, as it don\u2019t require special materials and things like that, his power shapes the reality of the invention and make it work basically.</div> </div> </div> </div>This part is literally not true. All Q-tech that replicates powers (anything Rank 3+) has exotic material requirements. The higher the rank, the more you require specialised materials that you can craft components from. If a nova wants to build something out of \u2018sticks and brute quantum\u2019, she\u2019s either (a) going to fail, (b) already has the brute quantum power and doesn\u2019t need the sticks, or (c) they\u2019re very special sticks and it\u2019s going to take some effort for her to get them and refine them to work in her q-tech device.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-08T05:47:10-07:00","id":1379463,"title":"","content":"I guess my memory played a trick on me.<br /> <br /> \u201cEven then, she is intelligent enough to bypass certain material requirements as long as she can find, or produce, a suitable substitute.\u201d<br /> I had in my mind something different from the phrase above. More like \u201cif you have scale above it you can ignore material requirements\u201d.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-08T05:56:13-07:00","id":1379466,"title":"","content":"The sentence you\u2019re quoting is clearly in a paragraph describing core-tech, not q-tech.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-08T08:45:58-07:00","id":1379479,"title":"","content":"Its actually on Mega-Crafting session (second paragraph) for Core Tech (what is even worse).<br /> <br /> But the idea is still valid, a Nova works on the materials to make then work outside of normal rules, and that's why nobody can make it work except other novas and even Novas can't replicate other novas works easily.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-08T21:51:23-07:00","id":1379614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1378841-prometheus-chamber-replication?p=1379260#post1379260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Probably not on their own, though. Figure that our genius Nova would need to team up with a proxy-level psion to do this.</div> </div> </div> </div>The obvious way to do this involves 2 psions and a mega-Int nova inventor. One of the psion would need to be a pretty powerful Telepath who could use Mindshare ***** (Override) as part of a Network to connect a skilled biotech inventor (likely an EK or QK) and the Nova, and allow both of them to share each others' skill and knowledge (you'd likely need a Proxy-Tier Telepath to be able to manage this with a Nova). Convince a brilliant and skilled Qin biotechnician to join this Network and I'd expect the process to take a while, but success seems exceptionally likely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":96,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/96-john-snead","user":"John Snead","date":". 04-09-2020, 12:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/96-john-snead","name":"John Snead","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar96_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-08T22:50:14-07:00","id":1379644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John Snead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1378841-prometheus-chamber-replication?p=1379614#post1379614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The obvious way to do this involves 2 psions and a mega-Int nova inventor. One of the psion would need to be a pretty powerful Telepath who could use Mindshare ***** (Override) as part of a Network to connect a skilled biotech inventor (likely an EK or QK) and the Nova, and allow both of them to share each others' skill and knowledge (you'd likely need a Proxy-Tier Telepath to be able to manage this with a Nova). Convince a brilliant and skilled Qin biotechnician to join this Network and I'd expect the process to take a while, but success seems exceptionally likely.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a pretty clever and in hindsight obvious idea!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T01:40:36-07:00","id":1379710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John Snead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1378841-prometheus-chamber-replication?p=1379614#post1379614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The obvious way to do this involves 2 psions and a mega-Int nova inventor. One of the psion would need to be a pretty powerful Telepath who could use Mindshare ***** (Override) as part of a Network to connect a skilled biotech inventor (likely an EK or QK) and the Nova, and allow both of them to share each others' skill and knowledge (you'd likely need a Proxy-Tier Telepath to be able to manage this with a Nova). Convince a brilliant and skilled Qin biotechnician to join this Network and I'd expect the process to take a while, but success seems exceptionally likely.</div> </div> </div> </div>And hope the Doyen don\u2019t learn of it at an inopportune time! \ud83d\ude09<br /> <br /> (Sounds like some plot hooks there.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T17:52:39-07:00","id":1379971,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1378841-prometheus-chamber-replication?p=1379710#post1379710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And hope the Doyen don\u2019t learn of it at an inopportune time! \ud83d\ude09<br /> <br /> (Sounds like some plot hooks there.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, once Aberrant it out, a nice high powered campaign could be some Proxy Tier psions, an a Mega-Int nova inventor work to reverse engineer a Prometheus Chamber and remove some of its limitations, while the Doyen try to stop them, and perhaps various other groups try to steal their research sounds like a great deal of fun. For extra fun, add in a Qin PC with a similar level of XP (although psion Tier, since Qin can't reach Proxy Tier), who is helping in return for help designing some method of enhancing Qin psi (naturally, the Qin PC would be the first recipient). For a Qin Prometheus Chamber, I'd let it raise their Psi and Telepathy to 6 dots, learn 2 dots in all Auxiliary Modes, and maybe give them the Psiad Edge Strong Mode in one of their Auxiliary Modes.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/96-john-snead","name":"John Snead","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar96_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T18:16:53-07:00","id":1379982,"title":"","content":"Bear in mind that reverse engineering something involves taking it apart to see how it ticks. I don't see any of the Psi Orders allowing anyone to take apart their Prometheus Chambers; at the very least, it delays their ability to use them, and they'd be taking the very real risk that whoever takes it apart won't be able to put it back together again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T21:14:12-07:00","id":1380023,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1378841-prometheus-chamber-replication?p=1379982#post1379982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bear in mind that reverse engineering something involves taking it apart to see how it ticks. I don't see any of the Psi Orders allowing anyone to take apart their Prometheus Chambers; at the very least, it delays their ability to use them, and they'd be taking the very real risk that whoever takes it apart won't be able to put it back together again.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most of the time - I'm not certain a VK would need to take it apart, and neither would a Clear - one of each, networked via a telepath could likely learn almost everything they'd need to. Also, the data Norca and the Chibs gained from regrowing the QK chamber would be a <i><b>huge </b></i>help.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/96-john-snead","name":"John Snead","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar96_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T21:17:02-07:00","id":1380024,"title":"","content":"I could also see a Mega-Edge existing that allows a Nova to analyze something (either mechanical or biological) and get an understanding of it without killing, harming, or taking it apart. It might not be a low dot edge, and it probably would have prerequisites, but I could see it existing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T01:33:20-07:00","id":1380055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1378841-prometheus-chamber-replication?p=1380024#post1380024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could also see a Mega-Edge existing that allows a Nova to analyze something (either mechanical or biological) and get an understanding of it without killing, harming, or taking it apart. It might not be a low dot edge, and it probably would have prerequisites, but I could see it existing.</div> </div> </div> </div>That makes sense, it sounds like a low to mid dot Mega-Cunning Edge to me. However, a nova trying to analyze a *really* powerful piece of noetic biotech would have some <b><i>serious</i></b> negative modifiers.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/96-john-snead","name":"John Snead","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar96_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T04:17:06-07:00","id":1380076,"title":"","content":"Another possibility--try and trigger a hammersmith or Galatea style event, only for psi's. You may not get the control, but you couldn't more psiads popping up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1458-newk","name":"NewK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-11T18:32:47-07:00","id":1508098,"title":"","content":"Sorry to necro but I had been thinking about this lately, but I think the secret ingredient of a Prometheus Chamber is that it requires a Proxy level Psion to create, and each Chamber is an extention of the Noetic Template of the proxy as how to guide the creation of a psion. Also remember that at the end of the day, Psions were made by the Doyen as an eventual dead-end of noetic evolution, so the real way forward are psiads.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1435-videopete","name":"videopete","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1435_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-19T01:09:41-07:00","id":1508863,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>videopete</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1378841-prometheus-chamber-replication?p=1508098#post1508098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and each Chamber is an extention of the Noetic Template of the proxy as how to guide the creation of a psion.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's some additional limitations in there, though- Doyen are significantly more versatile in their peak noetic abilities than psions are- the limitation of 2 dots at most outside of a primary aptitude and inability for a single psion to use multiple aptitudes together was imposed, not a limitation of Doyen noetic shortcomings. <br /> <br /> My question would mainly be what happens if you remove the limitations and dunk a latent- are you more likely to get a copy of Doyen abilities or an <i>extremely </i>upgraded version of psiad limits- three primaries at 7, secondaries at 5, perhaps.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26448-shalmaneser","name":"Shalmaneser","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-19T03:34:55-07:00","id":1508874,"title":"","content":"Notice that the Doyen are not as limited as Psions, but they too can\u2019t go up to 7 in all modes. They have a single Aptitude that can go all the way to 7, and the others are limited to 5 dots.<br /> <br /> Psiads have 3 primary, but they can have a single mode that goes 1 dot above (and don\u2019t need to be among the primary). I believe the best way is that at Psi 7 the Psiads can increase all Aptitudes up to 5, one single Aptitude up to 6 and 1 mode of that aptitude up to 7. That would be the full evolution of Psiads to Psion level of power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-19T11:14:31-07:00","id":1508912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1378841-prometheus-chamber-replication?p=1378928#post1378928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Doyen would oppose any attempt, and I do honestly believe that officially sanctioned attempts would be requested, if not enforced.<br /> Heck, I can see the Psi Orders wanting to have a spare/secondary chamber.<br /> <br /> The problem is, no one has a solid lead on duplicating/replicating key components of Doyen design.<br /> That said, I do think it is the kind of thing Palket would love to study and be involved with. Would probably result in a meteor to the face though.</div> </div> </div> </div>The best bet in old school Trinity would be the Edenite Novas being allowed to peek at the Upeo Prometheus Chamber. (Since few, if any, other Proxies would be likely to allow a Nova to study their Chamber!) A Mega-Int Nova might be brought in not because of Bolade wanting to replicate the Chamber, but because it's 'sick' and she's hoping for help curing it. Why is it sick? Some sinister person has infected random Teleporters with an engineered virus that has no effect on them, but affects bioware they come into presence with, over a long term, so that it isn't quickly recognized (and has a chance of going undetected long enough for one of the Teleporters to come into contact with the Upeo Prometheus Chamber). Why the Upeo? The sinister person wanted to field test the virus on an Order that lacked national backing or powerful allies (not counting the Edenites, which they didn't know much about). Mess with the Ministry, get China to the face. Norca, Orgotek and the Aesculapians are great at biotech, and would be most likely to detect it before it infected their Chamber, and / or cure it before it fulfilled their goal of making sure no more Psions are made.<br /> <br /> But the Mega-Int Nova being a Mega-Int Nova can't help but learn stuff about the Prometheus Chamber while attempting to cure it, and might even *have* to create a replica to replace the dying one. And in the process might learn about the limitations that the Doyen *built into the Chambers,* and be able to create one *without* those limits, and able to awaken any sort of Psion, and perhaps even *new* Aptitudes, unknown to current noetic science, like an Anti-Psi or Meta-Psionic Aptitude, or one based around Ectoplasmic Manifestation or 'Metacreativity' / Matter Manipulation.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23754-ian-turner","name":"Ian Turner","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-20T13:19:41-07:00","id":1509085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ian Turner</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1378841-prometheus-chamber-replication?p=1508912#post1508912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The best bet in old school Trinity would be the Edenite Novas being allowed to peek at the Upeo Prometheus Chamber. (Since few, if any, other Proxies would be likely to allow a Nova to study their Chamber!) A Mega-Int Nova might be brought in not because of Bolade wanting to replicate the Chamber, but because it's 'sick' and she's hoping for help curing it. Why is it sick? Some sinister person has infected random Teleporters with an engineered virus that has no effect on them, but affects bioware they come into presence with, over a long term, so that it isn't quickly recognized (and has a chance of going undetected long enough for one of the Teleporters to come into contact with the Upeo Prometheus Chamber). Why the Upeo? The sinister person wanted to field test the virus on an Order that lacked national backing or powerful allies (not counting the Edenites, which they didn't know much about). Mess with the Ministry, get China to the face. Norca, Orgotek and the Aesculapians are great at biotech, and would be most likely to detect it before it infected their Chamber, and / or cure it before it fulfilled their goal of making sure no more Psions are made.<br /> <br /> But the Mega-Int Nova being a Mega-Int Nova can't help but learn stuff about the Prometheus Chamber while attempting to cure it, and might even *have* to create a replica to replace the dying one. And in the process might learn about the limitations that the Doyen *built into the Chambers,* and be able to create one *without* those limits, and able to awaken any sort of Psion, and perhaps even *new* Aptitudes, unknown to current noetic science, like an Anti-Psi or Meta-Psionic Aptitude, or one based around Ectoplasmic Manifestation or 'Metacreativity' / Matter Manipulation.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Entirely possible, though obviously a quantum-empowered individual won't get the noetic components as easily a psi-aligned individual can. I'd increase difficulty when non-aligned person studies Powered tech and I consider the Prometheus Chambers to be Powered items.<br /> That said, the Novas Upeo have made contact with haven't even been in the same star system as their Chamber in 2e.<br /> <br /> Interestingly, we have a group that addresses my concerns and have the expertise in order to not only notice the primary restriction in the Chamber (the Doyen bypass) as well as the motivation and knowledge to know what it is. It involves a certain destroyed Psi Order, and I am too tired to put up spoiler tags right now. Not to mention if the Phobe Trust existed in any game, any of their records could be used as a resource.<br /> <br /> That said, the biggest &quot;limitation&quot; with Chamber is the one Aptitude specialization...and in universe this has been confirmed to be an actual genetic limitation that effects all species, not just humans. It is the whole &quot;channels/gateways&quot; thing that you can find in the psiad chapter of the &quot;Aeon Expansion&quot; supplement that the initial kickstarter created, though the throughline that informs my opinion on the matter is more of the implied statements in &quot;Under Alien Skies&quot;. It is hard to &quot;power up&quot; this as you need the right kind of channels/gateways to develop an Aptitude but if you don't have sufficient power capacity, you can't turn it on. The fact is, this is explicitly called out as the primary function of the Chambers on Latents causes me some concern as gaining proficiency in multiple Aptitudes would be a function of the channels/gateways. While blocking off said gateways may be how the Chambers restrict Aptitudes, damming the channels to focus the power into another gateway DOES seem like a legitimate way to enable someone with lower power capacity to actually use their power and become a Psion.<br /> Which in turn, implies that removing those &quot;limitations&quot;...reduces the number of people who could use said Chamber. And that said users might not need the Chamber at all, already being Psiads.<br /> <br /> Unless","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-21T01:18:07-07:00","id":1509149,"title":"","content":"Also, you have to reminds Lattent would NEVER become a psiad, so you may say it\u2019s limited, but it\u2019s a big step for a possible psi evolution. You had a few hundred Psiads, maybe few thousand maximum, and now you have hundred thousand possible psions.<br /> <br /> As I see the Doyens re kind of evil, but not on the way they helped humanity with the chambers. What they did to Bhurano is evil, what they did to bulls eye is evil, etc, but the chambers is kind of an absolute win for humanity.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-21T08:08:33-07:00","id":1509187,"title":"","content":"The thing about the Chambers is that the gift once given cannot be taken back. What i mean is the Doyen gave humanity tens of thousands of psi users and can't snap their fingers and undo it. The chambers themselves are also physically out of their control.<br /> <br /> I have no problem with the only one aptitude manifesting, though i think it would be cool if chambers 2.0 allowed a person to choose which of the aptitudes it awakens in them. Maybe not character choice directly but still like a single chamber can awaken any of the eight. <br /> <br /> I also think it would be cool if chambers existed upon Leviathans and in the heart of order cities, etc etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-21T11:30:41-07:00","id":1509219,"title":"","content":"We know from information about the Nippon government that psions and biotech developed by the psi orders contain unknown alien DNA. We also know that psiads who roll well enough detect something disturbingly alien about psions. We know from real life science that &quot;Neanderthal DNA could be associated with <b>autoimmune diseases, type 2 diabetes, and prostate cancer</b>.\u200b&quot; ( <a href=\"https://www.news-medical.net/health/The-Effects-of-Neanderthal-DNA-on-Modern-Human-Health.aspx\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.news-medical.net/health/...an-Health.aspx</a> ) It wouldn't surprise me if every psion is a subtle genetic time bomb waiting to go off, and the fact that the changes are in the DNA means the problems would be inheritable.<br /> <br /> Beyond that, the prometheus chambers install at least two psionic backdoors into psions that the Doyen can exploit, and Dr. Bhurano only knows about one of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-25T00:21:42-07:00","id":1509561,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1378841-prometheus-chamber-replication?p=1509187#post1509187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing about the Chambers is that the gift once given cannot be taken back. What i mean is the Doyen gave humanity tens of thousands of psi users and can't snap their fingers and undo it. The chambers themselves are also physically out of their control.<br /> <br /> I have no problem with the only one aptitude manifesting, though i think it would be cool if chambers 2.0 allowed a person to choose which of the aptitudes it awakens in them. Maybe not character choice directly but still like a single chamber can awaken any of the eight.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or maybe just steered one towards the aptitude one has the most 'aptitude' for. In older books, it was sometimes suggested that so-and-so had a decent latency for X and was horse-traded to that other Order to be activated in their tank, instead of the tank of the Order that first found them, so it's possible that some folk lean more towards telepathy, and others more towards biokinesis, or whatever, and that 'tank 2.0' would just open the person up to the aptitude that they were most suited towards.<br /> <br /> And <b>Shepherdboi</b>'s notion of the Prometheus tanks having built-in safeguards to allow the Doyen to remotely kill all the psions activated with them, and / or blow them up? That A) absolutely sounds like something they'd do, in their wickedness, and B) absolutely sounds like something they'd not even bother to do, in their arrogance (and end up regretting and devolving into blame and recriminations for failing to do, when human Psions turn out to be a problem...).<br /> <br /> (Or, C) they got too clever by half, and tried to arrange a technique to *subvert* the human Psions activated in 'their' Prometheus tanks, only it's a far trickier thing than just giving them fatal diseases lying in wait to be triggered by their alien masters, and there might be a way around it (and a certain percent of failure), causing it all to blow up in their face as it put Psions they thought were under their control in sensitive positions, where a 'cure' for their control scheme could turn them into trojan horses, with fresh personal grudges against the Doyen that just tried to hijack them...)<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23754-ian-turner","name":"Ian Turner","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-25T01:46:42-07:00","id":1509565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ian Turner</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1378841-prometheus-chamber-replication?p=1509561#post1509561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Or maybe just steered one towards the aptitude one has the most 'aptitude' for. In older books, it was sometimes suggested that so-and-so had a decent latency for X and was horse-traded to that other Order to be activated in their tank, instead of the tank of the Order that first found them, so it's possible that some folk lean more towards telepathy, and others more towards biokinesis, or whatever, and that 'tank 2.0' would just open the person up to the aptitude that they were most suited towards.<br /> <br /> And <b>Shepherdboi</b>'s notion of the Prometheus tanks having built-in safeguards to allow the Doyen to remotely kill all the psions activated with them, and / or blow them up? That A) absolutely sounds like something they'd do, in their wickedness, and B) absolutely sounds like something they'd not even bother to do, in their arrogance (and end up regretting and devolving into blame and recriminations for failing to do, when human Psions turn out to be a problem...).<br /> <br /> (Or, C) they got too clever by half, and tried to arrange a technique to *subvert* the human Psions activated in 'their' Prometheus tanks, only it's a far trickier thing than just giving them fatal diseases lying in wait to be triggered by their alien masters, and there might be a way around it (and a certain percent of failure), causing it all to blow up in their face as it put Psions they thought were under their control in sensitive positions, where a 'cure' for their control scheme could turn them into trojan horses, with fresh personal grudges against the Doyen that just tried to hijack them...)<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I was under the impression that it was closer to C. Stuff like a bypass for all resistance from Doyen Telepathic abilities, automated cloning of Clairvoyant visions (probably in what passes as a backup server), override for Electrokinetic, Telekinetic and Teleporting powers (probably with a telepathic switch), etc. Subtle stuff, since it would be easier to spot more overt &quot;safeguards&quot;. <br /> I don't think the Doyen had specific counter for Quantakinesis as it was brand new to them.<br /> These are still hard counters, but as they require, well, ACTION from the Doyen, a team of psion has a shot of doing something about it if they are in a confrontation against a Doyen. Rather than instawin against the players and dropping a meteor on the Earth just because it is the only way to be sure. Obviously the Psi Orders have killed off all the Aberrants on the planet by that point.<br /> <br /> As an aside, B seems unlikely. The Doyen most defining trait is their rampant paranoia. Not to say they aren't arrogant, but that their fear trumps it everytime. They were meant to Ascend but their fear doomed them and they are now terrified of being called to task by those who succeed where they failed, of dying before claiming their rightful place AND being subplantyed as the most powerful people in the galaxy. The fear their own children enough to put them to death, simply because the changes they have done to themselves means the offspring will be different from themselves.<br /> The Doyen are too afraid not to put SOME kind of backdoor safeguard in any gift. They crippled the development of the Qin in order to guide them to attack their enemies. The Chromatics got the Qin treatment on steroids in terms of their technology but they have had enough time to mess with their genome yet. But after the Chromatic succeed in wiping humanity out, it would be next on the agenda, if they don't just end the species.<br /> <br /> That said, there are people who are outside the notice of the Doyen who are making Chambers. I'd say that any government with half decent ideas on the subject have at least one classified research group working on it, even if most of the leadership don't know about it. The same would go for several private corporate interests. Ok, maybe not Nippon, but basically everyone else.<br /> <br /> Given that individual Chambers are, well, built/grown differently to the others to account for the different Aptitudes, such research would not be as compatible one would think. Stupid cybernetic psychic biotech with inbuilt specializations...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-25T09:06:39-07:00","id":1509590,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1378841-prometheus-chamber-replication?p=1509565#post1509565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I was under the impression that it was closer to C. Stuff like a bypass for all resistance from Doyen Telepathic abilities,</div> </div> </div> </div>As far as we know, the Doyen can't actually bypass telepathic resistance. Known backdoors are:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">From the Aeon core book: If a Doyen possesses someone who has been through a prometheus chamber, they can use that person's psi powers. Why bother using a deadman's switch when you can possess your patsies and use them to kill your other patsies while ruining their reputations? As per Prometheus Unbound, it is blatantly obvious that a Doyen is periodically possessing Alex Cassel, his wife knows something is going on, and the Doyen possessor is contemplating eliminating her. Since the Doyen possessor can use Cassel's Electrokinesis, that means it has access to his Subquantum Computing power, the infamous Cassel File, and ALL electronic records on Earth.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">As per a different Aeon supplement (can't recall which one), every time someone who has been through a prometheus chamber invents a new 7th level power, the Doyen instantly gain access to that power, provided they're able to use 7th level powers of that Aptitude. This means Quantakinesis is safe, but all the other proxy level psions are potentially adding more big guns to the Doyen arsenal.</div></div> </div> </div>\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-25T09:14:16-07:00","id":1509592,"title":"","content":"The second one is from Prometheus Unbounded (that introduced the personal 7th dot powers). I must add that it\u00b4s more like once the Psion learn the power, Doyen can learn it, not needing to invent them themselves, its not that they just get access to it. Psiads that somehow get to that level of power may be capable of inventing powers that the doyen cant just learn and need to invent them again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}